{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Unit key vectors (C-31), and a test's key (C-39) where a vector names a `test`. Each vector lists files (path, kind, text), the run key's fields but digest (base), a unit, and which files are units, sources and rest (C-30) and which it read; `expect` holds the digests of what it read, of the rest set and of the sources' paths (shape), and the key. [ADR 0095] A Cargo test binary's vector also lists `envDeps`, the `# env-dep:` lines of the dep-info its reads come from and the folders a value's roots are replaced from (`root`, `targetDir`, `buildDir` (named as the target folder), `cargoHome`, `toolchain`, `rustupHome`, `home`, each optional but `root`), and `env`, the entries they give ([name, value or null], sorted); `expect` then holds `env`, their digest, which its key holds. `tools/refdigest.py unit-keys` computes them independently; the Rust code must agree. [ADR 0096] A Cargo test binary's vector may also list `buildScripts`, its closure's build scripts' runs (`outDir`, and `output`, the text of the `output` file beside it), the values of the variables they declare in COMMAND's environment (`values`, a name absent is unset), the files a dep-info of its closure names (`path`, `text`; those under the target or build folder, and those in the checkout that are none of the vector's `files`, are keyed) and the folders as `envDeps` has them, and `scripts`, the entries they give (sorted); `expect` then holds `scripts`, their digest. A Go package's vector, or one of its tests', lists `getenv`: the repository's `root`, its tests' log (`log`) and the values of variables in COMMAND's environment (`values`, a name absent is unset), and `env`, the entries they give; `expect` then holds `env`.",
